export anchor Organization:
    meaning:
        An organization is the account that a studio on the Studio plan
        works in. It holds the seats, the shared projects, the billing
        owner and the plan. A person on Pro has a personal account and no
        organization.
    seats:
        An organization has at least three seats. Each seat is one person
        with a sign-in. The owner adds and removes seats.
    owner:
        Exactly one person is the owner. The owner pays, chooses the plan,
        adds and removes members, and sees the usage of the whole
        organization. Ownership can be handed to another member.
    roles:
        - Owner, who pays and manages the organization
        - Member, who names inside the projects they can see
    rolesOpen:
        Whether a third role, such as an admin who manages members but
        does not pay, is needed for the first version is an open question.

export anchor SharedProjects:
    meaning:
        A project belongs to one account. In an organization it is either
        private to one member or shared with the organization.
    rules:
        - A shared project is visible to every member of the organization
        - A private project is visible only to the member who made it
        - Any member who can see a shared project may add names, revise, and check domains
        - Removing a member removes their access to shared projects
        - A removed member's private projects are offered to the owner before they are deleted, and are never deleted without a message to the owner
        - Usage spent inside a shared project counts against the organization's allowance, never only against one member
    attribution:
        Every change in a shared project records who made it. The project
        shows who added or rejected a name.
    liveEditing:
        The first version is live. Two members with the same shared project
        open see each other's changes appear as they happen, with no lock
        and no copy to merge.
    liveRules:
        - A change reaches every other open view of the project within a second or two
        - A name added or rejected by one member appears changed for the others, marked with who did it
        - A note a member is typing is private until it is saved, so a half-written note is never shown to anyone else
        - A member never has to refresh the page to see another member's change
    liveSafety:
        No change is silently lost. Where two members change the same note
        or the same name within the same short moment, both versions are
        kept and one member is shown that the note has two versions to
        choose from. Every other change applies in the order it happened.
    liveLimits:
        Live editing needs a connection that stays open while the project is
        open. When it drops, the view says the project is out of date,
        catches up when the connection returns, and never shows a change as
        saved when it was not.
    personalAccounts:
        Nothing is shared without an organization. A Pro account holds
        only its owner's projects.

export anchor Membership:
    joining:
        The owner invites a person by email address. A person who does not
        yet have an account signs in through the invite, using either a
        password or a magic link.
    leaving:
        A member can leave an organization. Leaving frees the seat the
        member held. The owner is told, and the price is not charged for a
        seat that is free.
    seats:
        The number of seats is the number of people who can sign in to the
        organization. An organization cannot have more members than seats.
    failure:
        When a seat is used up, an invite cannot be accepted. The person
        sees a plain message that the studio has no free seat.
